title: The computer plays tactics
intro: Red's units take their own turns: they come at you, guard a spot, or hold their ground. No code.
project: Empty | Ambush

chapter: A charge and a tower | Stance
create: Tilemap
rename: Field
set: Tilemap.Tiles = 1111111111\n1........1\n1...11...1\n1........1\n1........1\n1111111111
select: Main Camera
set: Transform.Position.X = 5
set: Transform.Position.Y = -3
look: 5, -3, 4
deselect
create: Tactics Unit
rename: Knight
set: Transform.Position = 1.5, -2.5, 0
set: Health.Max = 5
create: Tactics Unit
rename: Orc
set: Transform.Position = 5.5, -1.5, 0
select: Turns
explain: field:TurnOrder.ComputerTeams | Red is the computer's | The first tactics unit set the computer to play Red.
select: Orc
say: This orc charges: it comes after the nearest foe.
explain: field:TacticsUnit.Stance | Stance | Its Stance says how the computer plays it: Charge comes at you, Guard waits until you come close, and Hold never moves.
create: Tactics Unit
rename: Squire
set: Transform.Position = 1.5, -3.5, 0
create: Tactics Unit
rename: Tower
set: Transform.Position = 8.5, -4.5, 0
set: TacticsUnit.Stance = Hold
set: TacticsUnit.Range = 3
set: TacticsUnit.MinRange = 2
say: And a tower that holds its ground and shoots anything that comes within three cells.

chapter: Red's turn | It plays itself
play
wait: 0.5
gameclick: Knight
gameclick: Knight
gameclick: Squire
gamehover: 2.5, -4.5
gameclick: 2.5, -4.5
wait: 1
expectvalue: Turns.TurnOrder.Current = Red
say: Blue's knight waits and the squire steps forward. Now it's Red's turn, and nobody needs to click.
wait: 1.2
explain: game | Its reach first | Before each of its units moves, its reach lights up, so you can see what's coming.
wait: 2.5
expectvalue: Turns.TurnOrder.Current = Blue
expectvalue: Knight.Health.Current = 4
expectat: Orc = 1.5, -1.5
say: The orc walked up and hit the knight. The tower had nothing in range, so it held.

chapter: Into the tower's range | Hold
gameclick: Squire
gameclick: 5.5, -4.5
wait: 1
gameclick: Knight
gameclick: Orc
wait: 1
expectvalue: Orc.Health.Current = 2
say: The squire walks into the tower's range, and the knight hits the orc back.
wait: 4
expectvalue: Squire.Health.Current = 2
expectvalue: Knight.Health.Current = 3
explain: game | The tower fires | On Red's turn the orc swings at the knight again, and the tower shoots the squire from where it stands.
stop
say: That's a computer opponent for tactics: give each unit a stance, and the computer plays its team.
